   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Talking about money",
     "texto": [
      "At home you earn a **sueldo** and you pay **gastos**: the **alquiler**, the bills, the food.\n\n- If you put money aside, you have **ahorros**.\n- If it is not enough, you ask for a **préstamo** and pay **intereses**.\n- If money runs short, you do not **llegas a fin de mes**.\n\nIn the **economía** of a place, **precios** go up or down. A country **exporta** what it sells abroad and **importa** what it buys abroad. From the countryside comes the **cosecha**; from the coasts, **turismo**.\n\nTo describe a change: **cada vez más**, **cada vez menos**, **ha subido un cinco por ciento**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "More and more, less and less",
     "texto": [
      "To describe how something changes, use these formulas:\n\n- **cada vez más** + adjective or noun: **cada vez más caro**.\n- **cada vez menos** + noun: **cada vez menos ahorros**.\n- **subir, bajar, aumentar, disminuir** + **un** + number + **por ciento**: **han subido un cinco por ciento**.\n\nNote: **cada vez más** never changes, but the adjective does: **los precios son cada vez más altos**.\n\nFor changes that reach up to today, use the present perfect: **han subido, ha bajado**."
     ],
